content.text:
## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/load_drop_retry.sh | ⚠️ important the watchdog poll timer busy spins 1 core for the entire lifetime of every attempt the new watchdog uses read t 1 u 3 with fd 3 opened from dev zero as its 1 second poll timer scripts load drop retry sh 170 181 reused at 195 199 for the drain loop read on dev zero never blocks and never yields a newline so the builtin loops on instant read syscalls for the full second — this is a hot poll loop not a timer measured on this checkout the real script stubbed runner 30 s wall run with a sleeping stub 30 25 cpu seconds consumed 8 20 user 22 05 sys ≈ one full core pinned for the whole run sampled at 3 s elapsed the wrapper bash at 99 3 cpu ps o pcpu while the stub itself slept at 0 why it matters this watchdog now runs on every attempt of every wrapped leg — the pty integration shards ci yml 1470 the core unit shards ci yml 1011 the jsr trio ci yml 1047 and the local fast gate ci fast gate sh 252 a healthy shard run pays one pinned core for its full duration a 5 min shard ≈ 5 core minutes stolen and the pty legs are precisely the load sensitive class fa pty budget scale sm dispatch waves pack the hosted pool whose flakes this pr heals — the fix adds sustained cpu contention to the conditions that induce the failure the intent behind dev zero killing this subshell mid wait forks no sleep child for the job harness to report can be kept with a true zero cpu zero child timer open a watchdog private fifo o rdwr — exec 3 console wdg fifo — an o rdwr fifo never eofs the process s own write end holds it so read t 1 u 3 blocks silently until the timeout verified in this sandbox 3 × read t 1 polls 3009 ms elapsed 0 00 cpu usr bin time 0 of wall add the fifo to the existing cleanup trap do not point fd 3 at the console fifo itself — reading it would steal the runner s output from tee alternatively sleep 1 would also work but forks the child you deliberately avoided so the fifo timer is the closer match to the stated constraint the ≤1 s drain loop at 195 is bounded and can keep the dev zero form or take the same fix |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

